  "faithful": "The gramme is a weight equal that of 1 cubic centimetre of water at its maximum density. It contains 10 decigrammes = 100 centigrammes = 15.434 troy grains; and 1000 grammes = 100 decigrammes = 10 hectogrammes = 1 kilogramme = 2.679514 lbs. = 2.204857 lbs. avoirdupois. Also 100 kilogrammes = 10 myriagrammes = 1 metrical quintal = 220.466 lbs. avoirdupois; and 10 quintals = weight of a cubic metre of water = 1 millier or marine ton = 19 Brit. cwt. 2 qrs. 20 lbs. 13.75 oz.",
  "modern": "The gram is a weight equal that of 1 cubic centimeter of water at its maximum density. It contains 10 decigrams = 100 centigrams = 15.434 troy grains; and 1000 grams = 100 decigrams = 10 hectograms = 1 kilogram = 2.679514 lbs. = 2.204857 lbs. avoirdupois. Also 100 kilograms = 10 myriagrams = 1 metrical quintal = 220.466 lbs. avoirdupois; and 10 quintals = weight of a cubic meter of water = 1 millier or marine ton = 19 Brit. cwt. 2 qrs. 20 lbs. 13.75 oz."
